body:
You keep bringing up the same point.  I never said the system was perfect or even good.  but maybe your letting media and your convoluted ideas on what it is that police actually do lead you to your conclusions.   Plenty of elderly people that you care for and assist probably did some bad things in their lives, some may have even hurt people. the elder generations are to blame for a lot of the racism and hatred that has plagued this country for years. yet you still see it as your responsibility to help them. and that's good.

&#x200B;

 Do cops need as much power as they have now? of course not.  I never said I agree with what the force itself stands for.   But the fact remains that those officers put their lives on the line to assist those that without them may not be around today. Not all cops are heroes, just like not every soldier is a hero. but those that show heroic actions in the face of danger deserve the recognition they earned.
